---
// EQ reshapes the frequency balance: an original curve (bright, lean) nudged toward a warmer, flatter
// result. Static teaching diagram for the EQ article. Illustrative curves.
---

<figure class="fig">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 760 316" role="img" aria-label="A bright, bass-light response curve and the same headphone after EQ — bass raised, treble tamed — with arrows showing the adjustment.">
    <defs>
      <marker id="eq-up" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="5" refY="1" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto"><path d="M0 8 L5 0 L10 8 z" fill="#FF9E2C"></path></marker>
      <marker id="eq-dn" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="5" refY="9" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto"><path d="M0 2 L5 10 L10 2 z" fill="#FF9E2C"></path></marker>
    </defs>
    <!-- gridlines -->
    <g font-family="var(--mono)" font-size="10" fill="#565b60">
      <line x1="44" y1="84" x2="744" y2="84" stroke="#1b1d20" stroke-width="1"></line><text x="37" y="87" text-anchor="end">+6</text>
      <line x1="44" y1="151" x2="744" y2="151" stroke="#34383d" stroke-width="1.3"></line><text x="37" y="154" text-anchor="end">0</text>
      <line x1="44" y1="218" x2="744" y2="218" stroke="#1b1d20" stroke-width="1"></line><text x="37" y="221" text-anchor="end">-6</text>
    </g>
    <g font-family="var(--mono)" font-size="10" fill="#565b60" text-anchor="middle">
      <text x="44" y="256">20</text><text x="230" y="256">100</text><text x="418" y="256">1k</text><text x="560" y="256">5k</text><text x="744" y="256">20k</text>
    </g>

    <!-- original: bright + bass-light (dashed, muted) -->
    <path d="M44 214 C160 205 260 162 390 153 C480 149 545 92 610 70 C660 84 706 122 744 150" fill="none" stroke="#565b60" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="6 5"></path>
    <!-- EQ'd: warmer + flatter (solid amber) -->
    <path d="M44 138 C160 143 270 150 390 152 C500 151 560 138 620 141 C670 145 710 149 744 156" fill="none" stroke="#FF9E2C" stroke-width="2.6"></path>

    <!-- adjustment arrows -->
    <line x1="104" y1="206" x2="104" y2="146" stroke="#FF9E2C" stroke-width="1.6" marker-end="url(#eq-up)"></line>
    <line x1="606" y1="80" x2="606" y2="138" stroke="#FF9E2C" stroke-width="1.6" marker-end="url(#eq-dn)"></line>

    <!-- labels -->
    <g font-family="var(--mono)" font-size="11">
      <text x="120" y="200" fill="#565b60">original</text>
      <text x="150" y="128" fill="#FF9E2C">after EQ</text>
      <text x="116" y="138" fill="#565b60" font-size="9.5">more bass</text>
      <text x="596" y="72" fill="#565b60" font-size="9.5" text-anchor="end">less treble</text>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>
    EQ reshapes the frequency balance &mdash; lift the bass, tame the treble &mdash; to move a headphone toward the
    sound you want. It changes <em>tone</em>, not the driver, the distortion, or the soundstage.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .fig { margin: 28px 0 0; background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 18px 18px 14px; }
  .fig svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
  .fig figcaption { margin-top: 12px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--muted-2); font-family: var(--mono); }
  .fig figcaption em { color: var(--muted); font-style: italic; }
</style>
